id: pmc-xndl
title: Track published pm-github apply-path limitations exposed by certification review
description: "PR #221 Greptile statically identified cancellation status omission, repeat export duplicates, closed-item status loss, project draft duplication after partial failure, and skipped pull-only default GitHub-preference changes in installed pm-github 2026.10.4. Generated installed distributions are removed from consumer Git scope; fixes and synthetic write-path acceptance belong in canonical pm-github work. This certification authorizes only read-only preview, which was a zero-case."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-04T12:10:47.382Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T04:08:23.855Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T04:04:13.283Z",codex-agent,"Current-main audit at aafea5d (package 2026.10.15): Still open; upstream implementation. Current caller `.github/workflows/pm-github-sync.yml:16` pins pm-github `2026.10.15` at `3015930b351a3d9c1c03ee4a26f8404025287df7`. That version's `index.ts:3904` still POSTs new exports without the planned issue state and does not persist the new issue link in that apply path. A newer pin alone does not prove the five limitations resolved. See design below. Design: Keep the current gated import caller separate from export and project-sync acceptance. In pm-github, use synthetic issues and a disposable project to verify canceled-item selection, create-then-close export status, durable issue provenance before repeat exports, resumable draft creation after a failed local tag/status write, and pull-only default preference. Persist remote identities before subsequent writes; retry from those identities instead of POSTing again. Require a second apply with zero duplicates and fault injection at each remote write/local receipt boundary. Adopt a published repair through the normal dependency/caller update once its nonempty acceptance evidence exists. These cross-system transitions exceed a small package-local change.  No item is closed; verification and closure remain with the orchestrator."
docs[1]{path,scope}:
  docs/backlog-verification.md,project
body: ""
